          "verdict": "issue",
          "quote": "English usually uses **'s** for people (*Kim's leg*) and **of** for things (*the leg of the table*), though **of** is also common with people in longer phrases (*the mother of the bride*). Words for amounts take **of** before **the**, **my**, **this**, and pronouns (*most of them*, *some of the bread*) but not before a plain noun (*most people*).",
